# Phase Frequency Detector & Charge Pump Testbenches

A concise, ngspice-friendly reference guide and testbench suite for simulating a **Phase Frequency Detector (PFD)** and an **Ideal Charge Pump (CP)** with loop filter load capacitor.

---

## Part 1: Phase Frequency Detector (PFD)

A Phase Frequency Detector (PFD) compares the phase and frequency difference between two input clocks: **Reference (`REF`)** and **Feedback (`FB`)**.

### Architecture & Operation

```
         +------------+
 REF --->| S  DFF1  Q |----> UP
         |            |
         | CLK    CLR |----+
         +------------+    |
             ^             |    +------+
             |             +--->| AND  |---> Reset
         +------------+    |    +------+
  FB --->| S  DFF2  Q |----+
         |            |
         | CLK    CLR |----> DOWN
         +------------+
```

1. **REF Leads FB:** `UP` goes high on the rising edge of `REF`. It remains high until `FB` goes high, which drives `DOWN` high. An AND gate detects when both `UP` and `DOWN` are high simultaneously and triggers an immediate asynchronous reset, pulling both lines low.
2. **FB Leads REF:** `DOWN` goes high first on the rising edge of `FB` and stays high until `REF` goes high to trigger the reset.
3. **Pulse Width:** The duration of the `UP` or `DOWN` pulse is proportional to the phase error:
   $$\Delta t = \frac{\Delta \phi}{\omega}$$

---

### ngspice Testbench (`pfd_tb.cir`)

This netlist uses ngspice behavioral digital primitives (`d_ff` and `d_and`) to model ideal PFD switching behavior:

```spice
* Phase Frequency Detector (PFD) Testbench
.title Ideal PFD Circuit

* --- Clocks: REF leads FB by 5ns initially ---
V_ref ref_in 0 PULSE(0 1 0 100p 100p 10n 20n)
V_fb  fb_in  0 PULSE(0 1 5n 100p 100p 10n 20n)
Vdd   vdd    0 DC 1

* --- Interface & Logic Bridge Models ---
a_in [ref_in fb_in] [ref_d fb_d] d_adc
.model d_adc adc_bridge(in_low=0.2 in_high=0.8 rise_delay=10p fall_delay=10p)

a_high d_one d_one_bridge
.model d_one_bridge pullup(load=1p)

* --- PFD Core: Two DFFs + Reset AND Gate ---
* d_ff nodes: D CLK SET RESET Q QBAR
a_dff_up d_one ref_d  0 reset_node up_d   un1 d_ff
a_dff_dn d_one fb_d   0 reset_node down_d un2 d_ff
a_and_rst [up_d down_d] reset_node d_and

.model d_ff d_ff(clk_delay=100p set_delay=100p reset_delay=200p ic=0)
.model d_and d_and(rise_delay=200p fall_delay=200p)

* --- Digital to Analog Bridge for Plotting ---
a_out [up_d down_d reset_node] [up down reset] d_dac
.model d_dac dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1.80)

* --- Simulation Setup ---
.tran 0.1n 60n
.control
  run
  plot v(ref_in) v(fb_in)+2 v(up)+4 v(down)+6 v(reset)+8
.endc

.end
```

